{% comment %}The report's findings panel. It swaps itself for a filter, a page, and a
saved triage decision.

Triage writes the VEX in the request but re-annotates the stored scan results on the
queue, so the decision reaches these rows in two steps: the save dispatches
refresh-assessments straight away, and reapply_vex_to_component_scans broadcasts
vex_reapplied when the re-annotation lands. Both arrive here as the same event. Without
this the modal would close on a toast and the row it was opened from would keep its
pre-triage state until the reader reloaded the page by hand.

The debounce matches the artifact page's: a workspace broadcast can arrive more than once
for one re-apply, and refetching the panel per message is wasted work.{% endcomment %}
<div id="scan-vulnerabilities"
     x-data
     hx-get="{% url 'sboms:sbom_vulnerabilities' sbom.id %}?{{ scan_refresh_query }}"
     hx-trigger="refresh-assessments from:body"
     hx-target="this"
     hx-swap="outerHTML"
     @ws:message.window=" if ($event.detail.type === 'vex_reapplied' && $event.detail.component_id === '{{ component_id }}') { clearTimeout($el._wsDebounce); $el._wsDebounce = setTimeout(() => document.body.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('refresh-assessments')), 500); } ">
    <c-tables.shell nested>
    <c-vulnerabilities.filters :panel="scan_panel" url="{% url 'sboms:sbom_vulnerabilities' sbom.id %}" target="scan-vulnerabilities" id="scan" prefix="scan_" push_url="true" />
    <c-vulnerabilities.table :rows="scan_panel.rows" :can_triage="can_triage" />
    <c-vulnerabilities.footer :panel="scan_panel" url="{% url 'sboms:sbom_vulnerabilities' sbom.id %}" query="{{ scan_query_string }}" prefix="scan_" />
    </c-tables.shell>
</div>
